Case Study: Alert Ease (Transit Tracking & Alarm Redesign)

Context-Aware Transit Alerts & Real-Time Navigation

Inspired by the core utility of Where is My Train, Alert Ease is a ground-up UI/UX redesign focused on high-stress commuting scenarios. The app reimagines destination alarm triggers, live transit status updates, and offline accessibility through a reduced-friction, glanceable mobile interface.

Project Type: Mobile App UI/UX Redesign

Inspiration / Benchmark: Where is My Train

Role: Product Designer (UX Research, Interface Architecture, Visual Design)

Tools: Figma, Adobe Illustrator

The Problem

Commuters relying on real-time transit apps often deal with visual clutter, unreliable network zones, and anxiety around missing station stops when resting or multitasking during long journeys.

Key Design Interventions

Glanceable Status Cards: Restructured live train progress tracking to emphasize current delay, next halt, and platform details at a single glance.

Smart Proximity Alarms: Redesigned station alert triggers using combined GPS and cell-tower data for reliable wake-up calls, even in low-connectivity areas.

Low-Cognitive-Load Hierarchy: Stripped away ad clutter and fragmented navigation in favor of a clean, high-contrast, one-handed transit UI.

